<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pathankot</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pathankot is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalayas</a> where the roads to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a> meet. The surrounding area was the land of the ancient Audumbaras, and the Pathania <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajputs</a>, who later ruled Nurpur, took their name from the town. Today it is an important railway junction and military base.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pathankot.jpg" alt="Pathankot" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vishalsaini at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pathankot_City_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
